Ran 8 tests across 2 files. [10.00ms]
```

Decisions the task did not spell out:
- `Bearer` match is case-sensitive (`bearer abc` is left alone); token is `[^\\s]+`, multiple occurrences per string replaced.
- Sensitive-key replacement wins over Bearer rewriting and applies to any value type (object/array/primitive → `'[redacted]'`).
- Only plain objects (`prototype === Object.prototype` or `null`) are cloned/walked; class instances (e.g. `Date`) are passed through by reference to avoid breaking them.
- `log()` redacts only `fields`, not `level`/`message`, per the wording “pass its fields through redact”.

